  "body": "Reported by the user (filed by an agent): on main after v0.15.0 (`d251029`), three snapshot tests fail with 23 differing pixels each:\n\n- `egui_app::tests::egui_shell_snapshot`\n- `egui_app::tests::egui_shell_snapshot_light`\n- `egui_app::tests::tool_editor_snapshot`\n\n**Cause:** the diff images (`crates/ui/tests/snapshots/*.diff.png`) show one glyph in the toolbar's top-right build label. `crates/ui/src/build_info.rs` pins the build time (`TOOLBAR_BUILD_UTC`) and the source sha (`short_source() -> \"test\"`) under `#[cfg(test)]`, but `toolbar_lines` and the compact label (`panes.rs`, `format!(\"v{}\", build_info::VERSION)`) still render the real `CARGO_PKG_VERSION`. The 0.15.0 bump changed \"v0.14.0\" to \"v0.15.0\".\n\n**Why the cut didn't catch it:** `scripts/release.ps1` runs the gate before it commits the version bump, so the snapshot suites passed on the pre-bump tree. Every future cut will turn main red the same way.\n\n**Fix:** pin the version shown in the toolbar under `#[cfg(test)]` (a fixed test string, like the build time and sha), regenerate the three snapshots once, and inspect them. The debug-info dialog test that asserts the real `CARGO_PKG_VERSION` keeps doing so.\n\n**Done means:**\n- The three snapshots pass on main.\n- A test pins that the toolbar label doesn't change with `CARGO_PKG_VERSION`: it renders the fixed test version.\n- The next version bump doesn't touch the snapshots.\n",
